35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The readmission data shows a fifth drop in over-seventies, but it reversed when the trial ended. The booking system misses unstructured care entirely.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The booking system only tracks named slots. Unstructured work vanishes from reports. That is a blind spot I cannot ignore.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The jointly run clinic collapsed because neither department owned the rota. The shared nursing round lost a third of visits to logistics. I need to know who actually commits long-term.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Nine posts are empty, and agency costs are climbing. But midwifery has slack! We could balance the load there.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The allocation is down a quarter, and fitting out is now charged to it. The data agreements took fourteen months. We must know the true running cost before committing.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, the booking gap confirms my fear. Unstructured care is invisible. We cannot measure impact if the system does not record it.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, exactly. If the work is invisible, we cannot manage the flow. The car park fills before eleven, so any new traffic will just pile up.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, midwifery slack is a lifeline. But if the arrangement rests on a partner who never signed up, it breaks in year two.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, I agree. But the therapy team is shrinking too. We need a program that fits the midwifery slack, not one that strains the empty wards.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, midwifery slack is a rare gift. But with the budget cut, we must ensure the running costs are covered, not just the initial build.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, the joint clinic failure proves that without clear ownership, the program dies. I need to know which candidate has a single accountable lead.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, ownership is vital, but if the shuttle only reaches four villages, the patients simply cannot arrive. I am checking the booking logs for overflow.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, the shuttle gap is a hard limit. But my data shows shared logistics fail when no one owns the rota. We need a single, committed lead.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, the shuttle gap is real, but the staffing is the bigger risk. We cannot add work to teams that are already empty.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, the shuttle gap is a hard limit. But with the budget cut, we must ensure the running costs are covered, not just the initial build.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
