60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"The readmission drop reversed when the trial ended. That is the pattern I fear. We need a program with clear, measurable outcomes, not just activity.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Candidate C needs a dedicated space. My data shows outpatient rooms are already full by mid-morning. There is no room for it.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Candidate B is a joint arrangement. My minutes show that model collapses when neither side owns the rota. I am deeply skeptical of its longevity.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Candidate B fits the midwifery slack perfectly! It uses the available staff, unlike the others which would strain our empty wards.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,Candidate D requires outside data agreements. My records show those take fourteen months. That is a delay we cannot afford with this reduced budget.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, the joint model is risky, but Candidate B has a single midwifery lead. Unlike the failed clinic, this structure has clear accountability.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, accountability is good, but the car park fills before eleven. If B draws new traffic, the physical space will seize up.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, the car park is a constraint, but the joint clinic failed because of ownership, not traffic. B has a clear lead, unlike the failed model.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, the midwifery team has slack, so they can handle the extra visits without breaking. The parking issue is real, but the staffing fit is too good to ignore.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, the staffing fit is vital, but the budget is cut. I must ask: does the perinatal service generate revenue to cover its own running costs, or is it a silent drain?","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, the perinatal service is scheduled, so it fits the booking system. Unlike unstructured care, its impact is measurable and the costs are predictable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, scheduled slots are the only thing the system tracks. B fits the infrastructure. C and D would create invisible work that vanishes from our reports.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, predictable costs are a relief. But I need to know if the pediatric side is truly committed, or if this is another joint venture waiting to collapse in year two.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, the midwifery team is ready and eager! The pediatric side is supportive too. We have the people, so let’s trust the structure to hold.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, the pediatric commitment is vital. But with the budget cut, I need to know if the running costs are covered, or if we are just deferring the debt to next year.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"I vote for B. It fits the booking system, uses available staff, and offers measurable outcomes. The others carry risks I cannot accept.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I vote for B. It uses scheduled slots the system tracks. C and D create invisible work that would seize up our already full infrastructure.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for B. The midwifery lead provides the single accountability my data demands. It avoids the joint-ownership trap that killed the clinic.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"I vote for B! The midwifery team has the slack to handle it, and it keeps our exhausted ward nurses safe. It is the only choice that truly works for the people.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"I vote for B. It is scheduled, so the costs are visible and predictable. Unlike the others, it does not hide its running expenses in the ledger.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
